-- title:
--   Finite Hopf algebra as a power of a local quotient
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field and let $B$ be a commutative ring carrying the structure of a Hopf algebra over $k$ which is finite as a $k$-module, both $k$ and $B$ lying in the same universe. The assertion is that there exist a natural number $n$, a type $B_0$ in that universe equipped with a commutative ring structure, a $k$-Hopf algebra structure making it finite as a $k$-module, and a morphism $\pi : B \to B_0$ of $k$-bialgebras (a $k$-algebra map that is simultaneously a map of coalgebras, Mathlib's `→ₐc[k]`), such that: $n > 0$; $B_0$ is a local ring; $\pi$ is surjective; and the type of $k$-algebra isomorphisms $B \simeq \prod_{i \in \mathrm{Fin}\,n} B_0$ is nonempty, i.e. $B$ is isomorphic as a $k$-algebra to the $n$-fold product $B_0^{\,n}$. Note that the final isomorphism is only asserted at the level of $k$-algebras, not of Hopf algebras, and that $n$ is not identified with any particular invariant of $B$.
--
--   This is the translation-homogeneity statement for a finite group scheme $G = \operatorname{Spec} B$ over an algebraically closed field: $G$ is the disjoint union of finitely many translates of its unit component $\operatorname{Spec} B_0$, the bialgebra surjection $\pi$ being the projection onto that component. It feeds the structure theorem presenting such a $B$ as a finite product of quotients of polynomial rings by ideals generated by powers of the variables, [`HopfAlgebra.exists_algEquiv_pi_mvPolynomial_quotient_span_pow_of_isAlgClosed`](thm.html#HopfAlgebra.exists_algEquiv_pi_mvPolynomial_quotient_span_pow_of_isAlgClosed).
